Daimon::executeWithSig (direct-call relayer path)
├── given a bound recipient-lock swap mandate
│   ├── when the session key direct-executes a swap routed to the account
│   │   └── it should execute (recipient receives output) and emit Executed
│   ├── when the session key direct-executes a swap routed to an attacker
│   │   └── it should revert with UnauthorizedExecution (sigil denies)
│   ├── when the session key direct-executes against an unconfigured target
│   │   └── it should revert with UnauthorizedExecution (default-deny)
│   ├── when the session key direct-executes the right target with a wrong selector
│   │   └── it should revert with UnauthorizedExecution (default-deny, selector-scoped)
│   └── given the mandate has expired
│       └── when the session key direct-executes an in-bounds swap
│           └── it should revert with UnauthorizedExecution (expired)
├── given a bound mandate and a 2-call batch
│   ├── when every call complies with the recipient-lock
│   │   └── it should execute both swaps and emit Executed
│   └── when one call violates the recipient-lock
│       └── it should revert with UnauthorizedExecution (whole batch, no call executes)
├── given a successful direct execution at a nonce
│   └── when the same nonce is replayed
│       └── it should revert with ExecNonceUsed
├── given a signed execution whose deadline is in the past
│   └── when submitted
│       ├── it should revert with Expired (before burning the nonce)
│       └── it should leave the nonce reusable (a fresh, valid-deadline signature succeeds)
├── given a ROOT signature over the execution digest
│   └── when ROOT direct-executes a single call
│       └── it should execute and emit Executed
├── given a BIND+execute signature (enable inline) over the digest
│   └── when the session key direct-executes a self-recipient swap
│       └── it should execute, bind the mandate, and emit Executed
├── given a signature with an unknown mode byte (0x02)
│   └── when submitted
│       └── it should revert with InvalidSignatureMode
└── given an empty batch
    └── when submitted
        └── it should revert with NotSupported
